 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>Use the following scenario to answer questions 7 – 10.</p>\n<blockquote>\n  <p>The function <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> represents the revenue in dollars the school can expect to receive if it sells <span data-math=\"220-12x\">220-12x</span> coffee mugs for <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> dollars each.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Here is the graph of <span data-math=\"f\">f</span>.</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Parabola on grid. Horizontal axis, price in dollars, from 0 to 20. Vertical axis, revenue in dollars, from 0 to 1000. Parabola opens down. Vertex near 9 comma 1000. \\(\\(x\\)-intercepts near 0 and 18 point 2.\" height=\"209\" src=\"exercises/media/13fbfce73d908db5.svg\" width=\"324\"></p>\n<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"7\">\n  <li>Select <strong>three</strong> statements that describe this situation.</li>\n</ol>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 654191,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol type=\"a\">\n  <li>At $2 per coffee mug, the revenue will be $196.</li>\n  <li>The school expects to sell 160 mugs if the price is $5 each.</li>\n  <li>The school will lose money if it sells the mugs for more than $10 each.</li>\n  <li>The school will earn about $1,000 if it sells the mugs for $10 each.</li>\n  <li>The revenue will be more than $700 if the price is between $5 and $14.</li>\n  <li>The expected revenue will increase if the price per mug is greater than $10.</li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
